    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_ab3125308086448b3dcb0ced2828af5659330fd11405e47c30d66cef6f604744",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A common analytic coefficient mechanism coordinates several Gaussian random-walk quantities: the alpha=1/2 specialization expands the expected ladder height and identifies the limiting overshoot coefficient, likelihood-ratio and renewal identities transfer it to boundary-crossing probabilities and correction terms, and other alpha specializations of the same continued Dirichlet series generate higher ladder-height moments and overshoot derivatives.",
